  "fixed-panel": {
   "note": "photo - ALARM DB-15 at the left, four fixed XE SFP+ cages at centres 97.8-140.6 silkscreened 2/0/0-2/0/3, SYS OK lamp and ONLINE/OFFLINE button, EXT REF CLOCK and ToD RJ45s at 269.9/285.5, the 1PPS / 10 MHz IN-OUT SMB quad inline at 311.5-334.2, and the junos badge"
  },
  "ground-stud-pitch": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "the hardware guide, grounding points specifications: 0.625-in. (15.86-mm) centres, which is 5/8 in., 15.875; the guide rounds the conversion. `ground-studs` is one placement of juniper/mx-ground-stud-pair-5-8@1, which composes juniper/mx-ground-stud@1 twice at exactly 15.875 (L116) and presents `stud-pair-5-8`, so one two-hole lug (generic/two-hole-lug-5-8@1) lands across the pair and the ring lug still lands on either stud, `ground-studs/1` and `/2`. The two studs were drawn 16.0 apart; they moved symmetrically about the midpoint the photograph placed, (205.0, 136.0), side by side, so a lug's wire leaves to the right, and their cutouts with them."
  },
  "ground-stud-size": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "the hardware guide, grounding points specifications: two threaded holes that fit SAE 10-32 screws, spaced at 0.625 in. (15.86 mm) centres, for one two-hole cable lug: the `stud-size` of both studs."
  },
  "lifecycle": {
   "note": "announced - MX104 is EOL (TSB seen in the family tables; image-library page redirects). Per-SKU dates on the Juniper milestones page"
  },
  "mic-bays": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "the four MIC bays are the MIC plate, 168.8 x 29.2 (#261), placed off the front photograph. Across, at 3.090 px/mm (body 74.5 to 1425.0 px over 437.0 mm, confirmed by the ganged-SFP pitch at 3.091): the left plates start at 129.0 to 129.5 px, 17.8 mm, and the right at 652.5 px, 187.1 mm, a pitch of 523 px or 169.3 mm, which leaves a 0.5 mm seam between 168.8 plates. Down, on the chassis-height scale (473.5 px over 154.7 mm, 3.061, the top at 9.0 px): the upper plates run 138.75 to 229.5 px (42.4 to 72.0) and the lower 235.5 to 325.5 px (74.0 to 103.4), and a 29.2 plate centred in each gives y 42.6 and 74.1. The slot legends sit beside the plates' upper thirds, as printed. Until 4.0.0 the bays were 168 x 27 at x 17.8 and 193.0, y 49 and 81 - a 175.2 pitch and rows 6 to 7 mm low. The rest of the front's vertical frame is not re-measured here: the fixed XE row centre reads 28.3 against a modelled 25.2, and the PEM/RE band starts at 105.2 against 108.7."
  },
  "other-faces": {
   "note": "left face carries the estimated fan-tray band (side-mounted cooling per the guide); other faces rail-band estimates. Axis conventions per viewer3d.js as the siblings"
  },
  "populated-with": {
   "note": "photo - slot 1/0 and 0/1 carry MIC-3D-20GE-SFP, slot 1/1 the MIC-3D-4CHOC3-1OC12-CE, slot 0/0 the MIC-3D-2XGE-XFP; both RE bays carry the slim MX104 RE and both PSU bays the DC supply. Defaults reproduce that configuration"
  },
  "power": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "guide power consumption topic, Table 6 - 600 W for the AC router and 625 W for the DC router, measured from the power source (INPUT side) on a system with redundant supplies, redundant Routing Engines and the fan tray, fully loaded with MICs; 325 W AC and 350 W DC without MICs. The guide labels all four rows typical; the MX104 datasheet labels the loaded pair fully loaded (max) and the no-MIC pair typical. Carried as power-max-ac-w and power-max-dc-w with that disagreement in power-max-scope; the no-MIC rows stay here and are not carried. The guide has no per-module power table: the MIC and supply contracts carry their own figures, and the Routing Engine has none (see gaps)"
  },
  "rear": {
   "note": "photo - a plain panel with the two-hole earthing plate at the bottom centre; nothing else. The fan tray and air filter are SIDE-mounted per the guide (Figure 7/8) and appear on the left face as an estimated band"
  },
  "scale": {
   "note": "photo - the front photograph is isotropic at 3.087 px/mm once the brackets are excluded (aspect with brackets matches the 48.7 cm over-brackets figure). Rows: fixed panel 0-44.4, MIC rows 44.4-76.5 and 76.5-108.5, PSU/RE band to 154.7. A FIRST READING put the RE rows at 13.9 mm - too thin to hold their photographed RJ45s - and the row boundary was re-derived; positions are single-pass and approximate to ~2 mm throughout"
  },
  "sources": {
   "note": "MX104 Hardware Guide, the MX104 datasheet, and the image-library photographs mx104-front-high and mx104-rear-high. No mechanical drawing was available"
  }
